  "summary": "Patch round 1, the open question answered A. Identity: the newest Claim: is still 6248725775, naming this branch. Amendment 6249110232 adds packages/lint/src/authoring-rules.ts to the file surface: only the comment above the validateFilterTokens registration. I posted no claim of my own. The worktree was recreated from origin/claude/issue-24293-filter-token-message at 6be194c50; the local and remote refs were equal and nobody else had pushed. No merge of main. One commit, f3d1666d9, comment text only. authoring-rules.ts :917-920 BEFORE: '#3574 — a filter value like `{current_user}` resolves in no vocabulary, reaches the data engine as a literal and matches nothing. The surface renders empty with no error, and a silent zero is indistinguishable from a genuine one at review time.' AFTER (:917-921): '#3574 — a filter value like `{current_user}` resolves in no vocabulary. The data engine refuses a query carrying it (`FILTER_TOKEN_UNKNOWN`, 400). When #3574 was filed it reached the engine as a literal and matched nothing: the surface rendered empty with no error, a silent zero indistinguishable from a genuine one at review time.' The #3574 provenance and the silent-zero history are kept in the past tense, as the module header has them. Pushed: 6be194c50..f3d1666d9. PR body: I did not PATCH it. The exact old_str/new_str pairs are in pr_body_edits below, 7 pairs applied in order. Each old_str occurs exactly once in the live body, which is byte-equal to the body sent at create. Applied, they give an 11097-byte body with no angle-bracket fragment, no control byte, and Fixes #24293 as its only closing declaration. A copy is at /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/af4ba868-8aa9-5ba6-91d3-488b25616713/scratchpad/issue-24293/pr-body-edits-r2.json, with the resulting body at .../pr-body-r2.md. The pairs: (1) the authoring-rules.ts table row goes from 'left' to 'rewritten in f3d1666d9', with the before/after blocks; (2)-(6) the Tests and Gates sections move to head f3d1666d9 and