  "pr_body_edits": [
    {
      "old_str": "| `packages/lint/src/authoring-rules.ts:917`–`:920`, the comment above the rule's registration (\"reaches the data engine as a literal and matches nothing. The surface renders empty with no error\") | **left**: the file is outside this card's claimed file surface. See Acceptance notes |",
      "new_str": "| `packages/lint/src/authoring-rules.ts:917`–`:920`, the comment above `validateFilterTokens`' registration (\"reaches the data engine as a literal and matches nothing. The surface renders empty with no error\"). The comment ships inside `@objectstack/lint`'s `dist/index.js` and `dist/runtime.js` | rewritten in `f3d1666d9`, comment text only. The claim's file surface was amended to add it (`6249110232`). The `#3574` provenance and the silent-zero history are kept, in the past tense, as in the module header. Before and after are below |\n\nThe `authoring-rules.ts` comment before (`21070a2f0`, `:917`–`:920`):\n\n```text\n  // #3574 — a filter value like `{current_user}` resolves in no vocabulary,\n  // reaches the data engine as a literal and matches nothing. The surface\n  // renders empty with no error, and a silent zero is indistinguishable from a\n  // genuine one at review time.\n```\n\nand after (`f3d1666d9`, `:917`–`:921`):\n\n```text\n  // #3574 — a filter value like `{current_user}` resolves in no vocabulary. The\n  // data engine refuses a query carrying it (`FILTER_TOKEN_UNKNOWN`, 400). When\n  // #3574 was filed it reached the engine as a literal and matched nothing: the\n  // surface rendered empty with no error, a silent zero indistinguishable from a\n  // genuine one at review time.\n```"
    },
    {
      "old_str": "On head `6be194c50`:\n\n- `pnpm --workspace-concurrency=2 --filter '@objectstack/lint^...' build`: `VERDICT command-exit 0`.\n- `pnpm --filter @objectstack/lint exec vitest run --maxWorkers=2`: `Test Files 144 passed (144)`, `Tests 6853 passed | 5 skipped (6858)`.",
      "new_str": "On head `f3d1666d9` (round 1's `6be194c50`, plus the `authoring-rules.ts` comment commit):\n\n- `pnpm --workspace-concurrency=2 --filter '@objectstack/lint...' build` (lint and its build closure): `VERDICT command-exit 0`. The old sentence's phrases (\"reaches the data engine as a literal\", \"renders empty with no error\", \"sent to the data engine as a literal string\", \"passed to the data engine\", \"matches no record, and the surface renders empty\", \"unresolved placeholder silently matches nothing\") have 0 hits in `packages/lint/src` and 0 in `packages/lint/dist`. The controls hit: the new comment's \"data engine refuses a query carrying it\" (src 1, dist 4 files) and the new message (dist 4 files).\n- `pnpm --filter @objectstack/lint exec vitest run --maxWorkers=2`: `Test Files 144 passed (144)`, `Tests 6858 passed (6858)`. The 5 cases that `6be194c50`'s run skipped (`6853 passed | 5 skipped`) are the `skipIf` cases in `lazy-deps.test.ts` and `runtime-lazy-deps.test.ts`. They need lint's own built `dist/`, which that run did not have. This time they ran, against the rebuilt `dist/`."
